# Database Rules

- PostgreSQL is the production database.
- Use migrations as the schema history.
- Never reset/drop production data automatically.
- Add appropriate indexes for high-frequency queries.
- Avoid N+1 queries.
- Use transactions for multi-step atomic operations.
- Enforce important uniqueness/integrity constraints at database level.
- Keep database access out of UI components.
- Use seed data only for development/staging as appropriate.
- Document schema decisions in `docs/DATABASE.md`.
